{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CONTEXT FROM a3fa's CI (patchset 1 Verified -1): the hazard is version-dependent, which is why ADR-0083 §193-198 was SAFE when written and silently became unsafe. Measured on the same proxy object and Protocol: python3.11 -> isinstance True (check is plain hasattr); python3.12 -> isinstance False (CPython gh-102433 switched to inspect.getattr_static). rebar's requires-python is >=3.11 and CI runs both, so an isinstance-only guard is correct on one supported interpreter and silently skips writes on the other. Any amendment should frame this as temporal decay with a version boundary, not an authoring error, and AC3's sweep should be run under 3.12+ — on 3.11 every proxy/MagicMock satisfies the check, so the sweep would find nothing."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786520952312581001,"uuid":"7003f885-1242-49af-9812-5c387530940e"}